description:
Design a clock divider that divides the input clock frequency by a specified factor, n. The module takes an input clock signal, clk, and uses a counter to toggle the output clock signal, clk_div, every n clock cycles. This allows for the generation of a slower clock signal that is n times lower in frequency compared to the input clock.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  output reg clk_div
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  output reg clk_div
);parameter n = 2; // division factor

reg [31:0] count;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  if (count == n-1) begin
    clk_div <= ~clk_div;
    count <= 0;
  end
  else begin
    count <= count + 1;
  end
end

endmodule

