Design a mask ROM (read-only memory) that outputs an 8-bit data word based on a 4-bit address input. The memory consists of 16 predefined 8-bit binary values, allowing addressable access to these values. When the address input is provided, the corresponding data stored in the memory is outputted, essentially creating a fixed lookup table for the given address space.
