description:
Design a circuit that converts a 4-bit binary input into a 4-bit Gray code output. The most significant bit of the Gray code is taken directly from the binary input, while each subsequent bit of the Gray code is generated by performing a bitwise XOR operation between consecutive bits of the binary input. This ensures that only one bit changes at a time between successive values, which is the key characteristic of Gray code.
module top_module(
    input [3:0] A,
    output [3:0] G
);

